roll for OS-9/68000===================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 1, roll, as posted.  roll.c buildsunchanged: the recipe gives -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand, since thedefault libraries have no random().  The post maps those itself, but onlyunder SYSV, which would also turn index() into strchr().Measured: every example in the post's README runs and prints in the formthe README shows.  Dice of one side are refused ("Dice must have at leasttwo sides"), as the source intends.  A refusal returns from main, so theshell sees status 0.Build: cc roll.c -DOSK -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand